n Europe","confidence":0.78}],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Adolf Hitler remained the key decision-maker, approving major escalations that transformed Nazi Jewish policy from persecution and expulsion into systematic mass murder.","confidence":0.98},"academicOrientation":{"score":78,"confidence":0.87},"profileConfidence":0.96,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"d135780abc40d54baea33c9623a5be80553834b638a7c3397b3225f2558bc9a5","reviewStatus":"flagged","validationWarnings":["central_places_hit_schema_cap"]},"summary":"In 1939, the Nazi regime's plans for redrawing the demographic map of Eastern Europe entailed the expulsion of millions of Jews. By the fall of 1941, these plans had shifted from expulsion to systematic and total mass murder of all Jews within the Nazi grasp. The Origins of the Final Solution is the most detailed and comprehensive analysis ever written of what took place during this crucial period -- of how, precisely, the Nazis' racial policies evolved from persecution and \"ethnic cleansing\" to the Final Solution of the Holocaust. Focusing on the months between the German conquest of Poland in September 1939 -- which brought nearly two million additional Jews under Nazi control -- and the beginning of the deportation of Jews to the death camps in the spring of 1942, Christopher R. Browning describes how Poland became a laboratory for experiments in racial policies, from expulsion and decimation to ghettoization and exploitation under local occupation authorities. He reveals how the subsequent attack on the Soviet Union opened the door for an immense radicalization of Nazi Jewish policy and marked the beginning of the Final Solution. Meticulously documenting the process that led to this fatal development, Browning shows that Adolf Hitler was the key decision-maker throughout, approving major escalations in Nazi persecution of the Jews at victory-induced moments of euphoria.","displaySummary":"In 1939, the Nazi regime's plans for redrawing the demographic map of Eastern Europe entailed the expulsion of millions of Jews. By the fall of 1941, these plans had shifted from expulsion to systematic and total mass murder of all Jews within the Nazi grasp. The Origins of the Final Solution is the most detailed and comprehensive analysis ever written of what took place during this crucial period -- of how, precisely, the Nazis' racial policies evolved from persecution and \"ethnic cleansing\" to the Final Solution of the Holocaust. Focusing on the months between the German conquest of Poland in September 1939 -- which brought nearly two million additional Jews under Nazi control -- and the beginning of the deportation of Jews to the death camps in the spring of 1942, Christopher R. Browning describes how Poland became a laboratory for experiments in racial policies, from expulsion and decimation to ghettoization and exploitation under local occupation authorities. He reveals how the subsequent attack on the Soviet Union opened the door for an immense radicalization of Nazi Jewish policy and marked the beginning of the Final Solution. Meticulously documenting the process that led to this fatal development, Browning shows that Adolf Hitler was the key decision-maker throughout, approving major escalations in Nazi persecution of the Jews at victory-induced moments of euphoria.","primarySubject":"Politics & Government","primaryTopic":"Holocaust","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Politics & Government","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Politics & Government","score":20,"evidenceCount":4},{"subject":"Race & Ethnicity","score":12,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"War & Military","score":12,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Biography","score":6,"evidenceCount":1},{"subject":"History","score":3,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Germany, politics and government, 1933-1945","mappedSubject":"Biography","s